EXTENSION "ArM5_Tales_of_Mythic_Europe_TheShipOfDesire_CaptainFolpertBerlensis" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, Tales of Mythic Europe - Captain Folpert Berlensis"
    VERSION "0.5.0"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-09"
    DEPENDS_ON "ArM5_Tales_of_Mythic_Europe_Core_Ext"

    # Captain Folpert Berlensis (Chapter Three: The Ship of Desire, p43): one character, its printed stat lines verbatim fields, its write-up the DESCRIPTION.

    #ta88884780775d79cd5e969 ^"Captain Folpert Berlensis" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tHoHTL05ExampleCharacterAA ^"Example Character"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Characteristics" STRING "Int +2, Per 0, Pre –3, Com –2, Str +2, Sta +3, Dex +2, Qik +1"
            ^"Size" STRING "0"
            ^"Age" STRING "35 (35)"
            ^"Decrepitude" STRING "0"
            ^"Warping Score" STRING "0"
            ^"Confidence Score" STRING "1 (3)"
            ^"Virtues and Flaws" STRING "Merchant; Ways of the Sea; Arcane Lore, Educated, Warrior; Enemies, Overconfident"
            ^"Personality Traits" STRING "Domineering (to crew) +3, Cheery (to passengers) +2, Loyal (transporting Pandulph) +1"
            ^"Combat" STRING "Dodge: Init +1, Attack n/a, Defense +4, Damage n/a Fist: Init +1, Attack +5, Defense +4, Damage +2 Bludgeon: Init +1, Attack +8, Defense +5, Damage +4 Short sword: Init +2, Attack +9, Defense +6, Damage +7"
            ^"Soak" STRING "+3"
            ^"Fatigue Levels" STRING "OK, 0, –1, –3, –5, Unconscious"
            ^"Wound Penalties" STRING "–1 (1–5), –3 (6–10), –5 (11–15), Incapacitated (16–20), Dead (21+)"
            ^"Abilities" STRING "Artes Liberales 1 (astronomy), Awareness 3 (weather), Bargain 4 (grains), Bows 3 (short bow), Brawl 3 (bludgeon), Carouse 2 (drinking songs), Dominion Lore 1 (saints), English 3 (navel terms), Faerie Lore 2 (water faeries), Flemish 5 (navel terms), Folk Ken 3 (port authorities), French 3 (navel terms), German 3 (market terminology), Guile 4 (lying about costs), Latin 4 (pagan authors), Leadership 2 (crewmen), Magic Lore 3 (vis), Normandy Lore 4 (covenants), Order of Hermes Lore 2 (covenants), Profession: Sailor 5 (coast of Normandy), Single Weapon 3 (short sword), Stealth 2 (hiding), Swim 2 (oceans)"
            ^"Equipment" STRING "Folpert usually carries his short sword in a scabbard at his side. He owns a full suit of chainmail, but keeps it in the hold with his other belongings. He has ten pawns of raw vis: 3 Ignem (rust-colored rocks), 3 Creo (dried rose petals), 2 Perdo (blackened fingernail), 1 Animal (rabbit ear), and 1 Imaginem (a small shoe). He also has a Platter of Hermes. This item is almost identical to the item held by Piccardo, and could be mistaken for it very easily; a magus would realize that both were made from the same Lab Text. Folpert uses his Magic Lore to find vis, and the Platter (which he bought with vis) to confirm his finds and ensure that he is not cheated."
            ^"Encumbrance" STRING "0 (1)"
            ^"Appearance" STRING "Folpert is a tad shorter than average, with large bushy eyebrows and sandy blonde hair, worn long. His face and arms are sunburned. He usually wears a blue tunic and yellow hose."
            ^"Source" STRING "Tales of Mythic Europe"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 43
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Folpert Berlensis is captain of *La main blanche*, which he has owned for ten years. Born in Oostkerke in Flanders, on the coastal plain near Bruges, Folpert grew up sailing ships and is an expert sailor. Lacking any national allegiance, Folpert transports cargo to suit his needs, and he is willing to skirt the local authorities in pursuing his business agenda. Pandulph has paid handsomely for discreet passage across the Channel, and Folpert is happy to oblige. Nothing in the negotiation said that other passengers weren’t allowed, so Folpert has taken additional people aboard. Pandulph won’t be happy about this, but is in little position to argue.\n\nFolpert deals in vis, buying, selling, and even stealing it for important customers. He has a few Mercere contacts that use his services, but is a relatively minor player in the Hermetic vis trade. His life as a sailing merchant is the perfect cover for this trade, providing the means and the excuse to visit ports located near covenants. As the story begins, Folpert has ten pawns of raw vis in various items."
    }

}
